import SwiftUI

struct PrebuiltModelInformationView:View {
    var body:some View {
        LessonRichText(text:"**Training and evaluation**\nFit learns only Training. Predict and Evaluate reuse a frozen package without refitting. Classification reports held-out accuracy, log loss, macro precision/recall/F1 and confusion counts. Regression reports MAE, RMSE and R²; undefined R² remains unavailable. Probabilities are not calibrated certainty.\n\n**Clustering**\nMembership describes similarity, not churn risk. Profiles use the prepared feature coordinates. Silhouette uses at most 512 seeded non-noise observations and reports coverage; fitting does not silently sample. DBSCAN is fit-only and has no predictive Model output.\n\n**Resource limits**\nPrebuilt numeric models run in an isolated CPU worker: at most 100,000 rows, 128 features and 2 million numeric cells; DBSCAN admits 2,000 rows. Forests admit 100,000 nodes, complete outputs 50 MB and model state 32 MB. Project limits also apply. Progress reports real phases where an algorithm has no iteration callback. Legacy document and Keras tasks retain their separate limits.\n\n**Results and saved models**\nPredictions, Assignments and Profiles use the standard tables. Connect View or Table Output. Numeric packages retain inert model state, ordered features and category identities; upstream scaling or encoding is not silently included. Supply the same prepared features after reload. Document packages additionally retain their frozen vocabulary and IDF. Original numeric/Keras projects keep their existing artifact and output contracts. No package imports arbitrary model code or provides optimizer resume.")
    }
}

struct GameSessionInformationView:View {
    var body:some View {
        LessonRichText(text:"**Rule and model binding**\nGame definition supplies authored deterministic two-player rules. The evaluator checks authored tests before running. Ordered observation expressions form float32 [1,N]; model output is [1,A] action logits. There is no implicit reshaping, normalization or tokenization. Candidate indices follow sorted action fields and their declared value order. The legal mask removes invalid actions without renumbering them.\n\n**Frozen episodes**\nCanvas definitions initialize once using their seed. Saved weights are verified against completed History and never reinitialized. Both sources remain frozen during episodes. Greedy ties choose the lowest index; sampling uses an independent seeded stream per entrant. Imported language/classifier models need a separately qualified game adapter.\n\n**Evidence and retention**\nMove/time limits are truncations, not draws. Summary and complete episode/move rows, definitions, model snapshots and provenance remain required. Optional decision details use the same 8 MB output allowance; reduce the batch or capture detail if it exceeds the limit. Recorded runs retain their original rules and weights. Use Train Self-play for learning rather than frozen episodes.")
    }
}
